<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Breck Sky Fest | Retro Science Festival</title>
<meta name="description" content="Two days of telescopes, solar science, mountain nights, and reasons to look up.">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css">
</head>
<body>
<header>
  <div class="wrap nav">
    <a class="brand" href="#top">BRECK <span>SKY FEST</span></a>
    <nav>
      <a href="#events">Events</a>
      <a href="#expect">What to expect</a>
      <a href="#partners">Want in?</a>
      <a href="#visit">Visit</a>
      <a class="button" href="mailto:Luke@AstroTours.org?subject=Breck%20Sky%20Fest%20partnership">Partner with us</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>

<main id="top">
<section class="hero sky-section">
  <div class="sky-decor" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/sky/sky-1.svg" alt=""></div>
<div class="wrap hero-wrap">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <span class="eyebrow">Breckenridge, Colorado · November 2026</span>
      <h1>BRECK<br><span class="y">SKY</span> <span class="p">FEST</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">Two days of telescopes, solar science, mountain nights, and very good reasons to look up.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="#events">Pick your sky ↓</a>
        <a class="button pink" href="#partners">Want in?</a>
      </div>
      <div class="stamps">
        <span class="stamp">Inaugural festival</span>
        <span class="stamp">4 programs</span>
        <span class="stamp">Sunlight → starlight</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="marquee">
  <div class="track">
    <span>Solar Lab</span><span>Night Shift</span><span>Telescopes</span><span>Mountain Sky</span><span>Breck Sky School</span><span>Breck Sky Night</span><span>Breck Sky Day</span><span>Breck Sky Summit</span>
    <span>Solar Lab</span><span>Night Shift</span><span>Telescopes</span><span>Mountain Sky</span>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="intro sky-section">
  <div class="sky-decor" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/sky/sky-2.svg" alt=""></div>
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow" style="background:var(--blue)">What is this?</span>
      <h2>A whole weekend built around the sky.</h2>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="large">Breck Sky Fest is a new astronomy and dark-sky festival designed to make Breckenridge feel a little more like an observatory, a science fair, and a mountain party all at once.</p>
      <p>The inaugural weekend moves from student science and solar observing into public telescope nights and a signature high-country stargazing experience.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="expect" id="expect">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow" style="background:var(--green)">What to expect</span>
    <h2>Do astronomy. Don’t just hear about it.</h2>
    <div class="cards3">
      <div class="card" style="--accent:var(--yellow)"><div class="num">01</div><h3>Look at the Sun</h3><p>Safely observe the Sun through dedicated solar telescopes and see features you cannot see with the naked eye.</p></div>
      <div class="card" style="--accent:var(--blue)"><div class="num">02</div><h3>Look through telescopes</h3><p>See planets, stars, clusters, galaxies, and objects selected for the actual November sky.</p></div>
      <div class="card" style="--accent:var(--pink)"><div class="num">03</div><h3>Learn the sky</h3><p>Find constellations, understand what you are seeing, and leave knowing more than when you arrived.</p></div>
      <div class="card" style="--accent:var(--green)"><div class="num">04</div><h3>Play with light</h3><p>Use spectra, optics, scale models, and hands-on demonstrations to make invisible astronomy tangible.</p></div>
      <div class="card" style="--accent:var(--orange)"><div class="num">05</div><h3>Get warm</h3><p>Mountain astronomy is cold. Warm-up spaces, drinks, and hospitality can be part of the experience.</p></div>
      <div class="card" style="--accent:var(--purple)"><div class="num">06</div><h3>Go higher</h3><p>The signature Saturday night is designed as the premium high-country experience of the festival.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="events" id="events">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow" style="background:var(--pink);color:#fff">Pick your sky</span>
    <h2>Four programs. Four reasons to show up.</h2>
    <div class="eventgrid">
      <article class="event" style="--accent:var(--yellow)"><small>Friday · Daytime · Solar Lab</small><h3>Breck Sky School</h3><p>Hands-on astronomy for students with solar observing, spectroscopy, light, color, and science they can test themselves.</p><span class="pill">Best for students</span></article>
      <article class="event" style="--accent:var(--blue)"><small>Friday · Evening · Night Shift</small><h3>Breck Sky Night</h3><p>The community telescope night: astronomers, constellations, planets, deep-sky objects, and an easy way to wander into the universe.</p><span class="pill">Best for everyone</span></article>
      <article class="event" style="--accent:var(--green)"><small>Saturday · Afternoon · Field Lab</small><h3>Breck Sky Day</h3><p>Solar telescopes, optics, scale models, light, color, and things you can poke, test, and look through.</p><span class="pill">Best for families</span></article>
      <article class="event" style="--accent:var(--pink)"><small>Saturday · Evening · Summit Session</small><h3>Breck Sky Summit</h3><p>Limited-capacity mountain stargazing with telescopes, astronomers, warm drinks, and the high-country sky overhead.</p><span class="pill">Best for the full experience</span></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="guide sky-section">
  <div class="sky-decor" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/sky/sky-3.svg" alt=""></div>
  <div class="wrap guidegrid">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Field guide</span>
      <h2>Four things can change the whole night.</h2>
      <p>Mountain astronomy is part science, part weather watching, and part being prepared.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="guide-row"><strong>Moon</strong><p>Changes how dark the sky looks and which deep-sky objects stand out best.</p></div>
      <div class="guide-row"><strong>Cloud</strong><p>Can turn a perfect observing plan into a waiting game.</p></div>
      <div class="guide-row"><strong>Smoke</strong><p>Can affect transparency even when the sky looks technically clear.</p></div>
      <div class="guide-row"><strong>Road</strong><p>Mountain access matters. Venue and transportation details will be part of every event listing.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="why sky-section">
  <div class="sky-decor" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/sky/sky-4.svg" alt=""></div>
  <div class="wrap whygrid">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow" style="background:var(--blue)">Why Breckenridge?</span>
      <h2>The place is part of the program.</h2>
      <p class="large">Breck Sky Fest is meant to feel specific to Breckenridge, not like a telescope event dropped into any town.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="whycards">
      <div class="whycard" style="--accent:var(--yellow)"><h3>Dark-sky identity</h3><p>A direct way to experience why responsible lighting and dark skies matter.</p></div>
      <div class="whycard" style="--accent:var(--blue)"><h3>Mountain atmosphere</h3><p>Cold air, elevation, open horizons, and alpine landscape become part of the experience.</p></div>
      <div class="whycard" style="--accent:var(--pink)"><h3>Science tourism</h3><p>An educational, memorable reason to experience Breckenridge differently.</p></div>
      <div class="whycard" style="--accent:var(--green)"><h3>All-day astronomy</h3><p>Solar viewing and hands-on science mean the festival does not wait until dark.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="audience">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Who is this for?</span>
    <h2>Basically anyone willing to look up.</h2>
    <div class="audgrid">
      <div class="aud"><div class="icon">☄</div><h3>Families</h3><p>Daytime science, telescopes, and approachable programs.</p></div>
      <div class="aud"><div class="icon">✦</div><h3>Science nerds</h3><p>Real observing, spectra, optics, and people happy to go deeper.</p></div>
      <div class="aud"><div class="icon">△</div><h3>Mountain people</h3><p>A new reason to experience Breckenridge after dark.</p></div>
      <div class="aud"><div class="icon">☕</div><h3>Curious humans</h3><p>No telescope experience required. Show up curious.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="flow sky-section">
  <div class="sky-decor" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/sky/sky-5.svg" alt=""></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow" style="background:var(--pink);color:#fff">Festival flow</span>
    <h2>Start with the Sun. End under the stars.</h2>
    <div class="flowgrid">
      <div class="stop"><div class="dot" style="--accent:var(--yellow)">01</div><h3>Learn</h3><p>Students start with solar science, light, and spectra.</p></div>
      <div class="stop"><div class="dot" style="--accent:var(--blue)">02</div><h3>Gather</h3><p>The community comes together for a telescope night.</p></div>
      <div class="stop"><div class="dot" style="--accent:var(--green)">03</div><h3>Explore</h3><p>Saturday turns astronomy into a daytime festival.</p></div>
      <div class="stop"><div class="dot" style="--accent:var(--pink)">04</div><h3>Go up</h3><p>The weekend finishes with the signature mountain session.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="partners" id="partners">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow" style="background:var(--green)">Want in?</span>
    <h2>Bring telescopes. Bring cocoa. Bring weird ideas.</h2>
    <p class="large" style="max-width:760px">We are looking for organizations that can make one piece of the first festival possible, smarter, warmer, easier, or more memorable.</p>
    <div class="partnergrid">
      <div class="partner" style="--accent:#ffe39a"><div class="label">Support</div><h3>Founding sponsors</h3><p>Help underwrite public astronomy, student access, staffing, equipment, or transportation.</p><a href="mailto:Luke@AstroTours.org?subject=Breck%20Sky%20Fest%20sponsorship">Sponsor something →</a></div>
      <div class="partner" style="--accent:#cfeef4"><div class="label">Place</div><h3>Venues + hosts</h3><p>Hotels, resorts, restaurants, outdoor spaces, and community venues.</p><a href="mailto:Luke@AstroTours.org?subject=Breck%20Sky%20Fest%20venue">Give us a home →</a></div>
      <div class="partner" style="--accent:#efc3cf"><div class="label">Science</div><h3>Astronomers + groups</h3><p>Bring telescopes, demos, observatory connections, astrophotography, or a great science activity.</p><a href="mailto:Luke@AstroTours.org?subject=Breck%20Sky%20Fest%20astronomy%20partner">Bring science →</a></div>
      <div class="partner" style="--accent:#d8ebca"><div class="label">Festival</div><h3>Vendors + makers</h3><p>Warm drinks, food, local products, art, outdoor brands, or science gear.</p><a href="mailto:Luke@AstroTours.org?subject=Breck%20Sky%20Fest%20vendor">Set up shop →</a></div>
      <div class="partner" style="--accent:#ffd2b9"><div class="label">Education</div><h3>Schools + youth groups</h3><p>Help shape Breck Sky School and give students a direct role in year one.</p><a href="mailto:Luke@AstroTours.org?subject=Breck%20Sky%20School">Bring students →</a></div>
      <div class="partner" style="--accent:#e2d4ef"><div class="label">Community</div><h3>Local organizations</h3><p>Nonprofits, wellness groups, artists, storytellers, and anyone with a complementary idea.</p><a href="mailto:Luke@AstroTours.org?subject=Breck%20Sky%20Fest%20community%20partner">Pitch us something →</a></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="visit" id="visit">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow" style="background:var(--blue)">Visit Breckenridge</span>
      <h2>Come for the mountains. Stay for the universe.</h2>
      <p class="large">As partners are confirmed, this becomes the weekend field guide for lodging, transport, mountain access, warm-up spots, and more.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="visitbox">
      <div class="visitgrid">
        <div class="visititem" style="--accent:#ffe39a"><b>Sleep</b><span>Festival lodging + hotel partners</span></div>
        <div class="visititem" style="--accent:#cfeef4"><b>Move</b><span>Parking, shuttles + mountain access</span></div>
        <div class="visititem" style="--accent:#efc3cf"><b>Layer up</b><span>Cold-weather stargazing guide</span></div>
        <div class="visititem" style="--accent:#d8ebca"><b>Refuel</b><span>Food, drinks + local partners</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="faq sky-section">
  <div class="sky-decor" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/sky/sky-6.svg" alt=""></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Good questions</span>
    <h2>Before you look up.</h2>
    <details open><summary>When is Breck Sky Fest?</summary><p>The inaugural festival is planned for November 2026. Exact dates will be announced after venue coordination.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Will events be free?</summary><p>The working plan combines free community programming with a ticketed signature experience.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Do I need to know astronomy?</summary><p>No. It is being designed for first-time telescope users and experienced sky-watchers alike.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can my business or organization participate?</summary><p>Yes. Sponsors, venues, astronomers, schools, vendors, local businesses, and community organizations are invited to reach out.</p></details>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cta">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Year one</span>
      <h2>Want to help make this weird, smart, and memorable?</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="ctabox">
      <p>Tell us who you are, what you do, and what kind of idea you want to bring to Breck Sky Fest.</p>
      <a class="button dark" href="mailto:Luke@AstroTours.org?subject=Breck%20Sky%20Fest%20partnership">Luke@AstroTours.org</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</main>

